  "notes": "Funk-and-soul-inflected pop-rock with a falsetto lead over a played rhythm section: 95–120 straight with the backbeat on 2&4 and a 16th funk subdivision. The claim that decides the drum block is \"funk-drummer ghost-note vocabulary is central to the feel\", so `ghost.prob` sits at 0.42 across four sixteenth positions — by far the busiest ghost pattern in this section. The other two deltas are quoted: \"kick on 1 and the '&' of 2\" and \"hat in 16ths with a foot-splash on 4&\", which is the `pedalHat` lane. Percussion is \"both programmed and live\", which is the one warrant for loosening `humanize`. Harmony is C-minor functional writing — i–iv–V and i–VI–III–VII \"with 7ths and 9ths; verses often on a two-chord vamp, chorus opening into a full cycle\" — so the triad share drops to 0.34 and the harmonic rhythm carries both a vamp and a per-bar option. The bass is the entry's sharpest instrumental claim and is encoded literally: \"syncopated 16ths, muted staccato notes with a slide into the downbeat; locked with the clavinet/electric-piano **rather than the kick**\", which is `independent_riff` at 0.55 with a real glide and a high anticipation. The lead has \"a wide leap into the hook\" and the \"chirping high backing vocals\" are the answer-lick counter. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are all drum probabilities and the humanize values.",
